&lt;h1&gt;


  Behavioral thermodynamics: a LoRA behavior melts at 3.5× its RMS noise
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is a physics-flavoured robustness probe, not a container. Take a fine-tuned behavior,&lt;br&gt;
add Gaussian noise to every LoRA tensor, and measure the order parameter: SST-2 accuracy on&lt;br&gt;
400 rows.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reproduce:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;python research/thermodynamics.py   &lt;span class="c"&gt;# -&amp;gt; research/results/thermodynamics.json&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


  Setup
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Host: 4-bit Qwen3B.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Behavior: SST-2 sentiment adapter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Noise: &lt;code&gt;w + N(0, (σ · RMS)^2)&lt;/code&gt; on every LoRA A/B tensor, one seed per σ.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adapter RMS: &lt;strong&gt;0.016192&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Metric: label-token logit accuracy on 400 SST-2 test rows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

