&lt;p&gt;Every small business has tasks that repeat on a clock: the Monday inbox sweep, the Friday invoice check, the weekly summary nobody enjoys writing. They are not hard — they are just always there. That is exactly what scheduled workflows in aiFetchly are for.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What a scheduled workflow does
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You set a task once, with a time and a trigger, and aiFetchly runs it on schedule on your own computer. For example:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Morning triage (every weekday, 9:00):&lt;/strong&gt; scan new customer mail, sort it by urgency, and draft replies from your local business knowledge base — so you start the day with a prioritised list, not a pile of unread mail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Weekly document round-up (every Friday):&lt;/strong&gt; collect the week's invoices and contracts, sort them into folders, and pull out the key details — amounts, dates, parties — into a short summary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Recurring reports:&lt;/strong&gt; prepare a draft weekly summary from your documents and notes, ready for a human to check and send.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Nothing is sent automatically. A human reviews every draft before anything goes out.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Why local-first matters here
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Scheduled work touches your real business data — customer mail, invoices, internal notes. aiFetchly runs locally, and your business knowledge base stays on your own computer. The agent works with your own documents and your own email, Sheets and CRM connections (via plugins), rather than uploading your business to a cloud service.&lt;/p&gt;

